v4l2-kernel/ holds userspace V4L2 ABI headers copied from the generated
kernel headers:

  out/target/product/gvwifi/obj/KERNEL_OBJ/usr/include/linux/{videodev2.h,\
  videodev2_exynos_camera.h,videodev2_exynos_media.h}

Source: kernel/samsung/exynos7580-common, include/uapi/linux/.

Why copies instead of -I <KERNEL_OBJ>/usr/include/linux:
Samsung's camera sources #include <videodev2.h> (bare name). Adding
usr/include/linux to the include path would shadow bioniclibc headers
(limits.h, time.h, types.h, ... lives there too) and break the build.
The copies expose only the three V4L2 headers; their internal
<linux/...> includes still resolve via KERNEL_OBJ/usr/include.

NOTE: 75xx/ ships its own tuned videodev2_exynos_camera.h and its -I
entry precedes this directory, so the 75xx copy wins for that header.
Regenerate these copies with: make INSTALLED_KERNEL_HEADERS, then copy
the three files again.
